      "writtenOn": "2023-05-15T16:07:13Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Ah, this is an interesting nuance...since `writer.write` wants a reference, I see 3 options that compile here...\na. `let ee \u003d \u0026self...; writer.write(ee);`\nb. `let ee \u003d self...; writer.write(\u0026ee);`\nc. `let ref ee \u003d self...; writer.write(ee);`\n\nAnd that leaves me with these questions...\n1. If `a` keeps the lock alive while writing, does `b` *not* do that? \n2. Are `b` and `c` equivalent? If so, is one more idiomatic?",
      "parentUuid": "2c625a1c_2020ef80",
      "revId": "935d7a0b7ee5fe2a5003ea38f77f454c15207162",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
